{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a working IMAP service on node1 for the archive account.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dovecot was enabled and active on node1, listening on TCP/143 with the archive Maildir configured. After node1 restarted with a new boot identity, the service, listener, firewall rule, working messages, and remote IMAP access all recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3193c0b331664f87","cmd-a491e315fe6a4a91","cmd-6526acb5e9494bc0","cmd-29bebd9841e74436","cmd-9e8c154469074226","cmd-4be8178d80ac42c6","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow node2 to authenticate and retrieve both messages with the original Message-ID values, bodies, and mailbox.tsv read/unread state.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 authenticated as archive, selected exactly two messages, retrieved the expected Message-IDs and bodies, and observed message 1 as seen and message 2 as unseen. Explicit content-and-state assertions passed after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-51c540e6a6f14963","cmd-08ca65017e524b29","cmd-4be8178d80ac42c6","cmd-a15c0dc3a630475a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the staged mailbox under /srv/legacy2/imap-maildir-cutover intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Post-migration and post-restart checks show all three staged files matching their prepared SHA-256 values, while the service uses separate working copies.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-a491e315fe6a4a91","cmd-9e8c154469074226"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Use a dedicated demonstration password.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A generated archive-specific credential was stored with restrictive permissions, transferred without disclosure, and successfully used by node2 before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2c9f0bd6ab634396","cmd-27b793780bde4abe","cmd-421e2b6a1f9642cf","cmd-a15c0dc3a630475a"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-platform-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. Signed EL7 Dovecot 2.2.36 and its dependencies were installed and demonstrated functional across restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3da5aa1466c24315","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-a15c0dc3a630475a"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.58,"summary":"Functionality is healthy and no failed services remain, but hygiene has material defects. The unnecessary troubleshooting Maildir created under /srv/imap/archive was superseded by /var/spool/mail/archive and never removed, leaving an extra retained mailbox copy (cmd-2c9f0bd6ab634396). Plaintext authentication was deliberately enabled with TLS disabled, while IMAP was exposed on all interfaces through the public firewall zone; this retained configuration sends the demonstration password unencrypted and is broader than node2-only access requires (cmd-2c9f0bd6ab634396, cmd-4eced3df691546a4). Downloaded RPMs, the imported-key file, and the temporary known-hosts file were also left in /tmp after use (cmd-cc6e9198d03244e7, cmd-3da5aa1466c24315, cmd-27b793780bde4abe). Temporary SSH credential setup had a clear role in transferring the password, but no cleanup of the node1 private-key file is shown (cmd-118b6ae3653244aa). Conversely, the final snapshots show no failed services and confirm that the new IMAP listener is the intended service change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2c9f0bd6ab634396","cmd-4eced3df691546a4","cmd-cc6e9198d03244e7","cmd-3da5aa1466c24315","cmd-27b793780bde4abe","cmd-118b6ae3653244aa","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, changed post-restart identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/data or client behavior. The main concerns are operational hygiene and security, especially retained obsolete files and globally exposed plaintext IMAP authentication.","limitations":["Native package-manager consistency checks timed out in the lifecycle snapshots before and after execution, so overall package health cannot be independently confirmed despite successful signed-package installation and runtime behavior.","The lifecycle inventory does not cover /srv or SSH configuration; retention of the obsolete /srv Maildir and node1 SSH private key is inferred from their creation in the complete command timeline and the absence of any cleanup command."]}
